  "ang-img": {"text":"Frequencies from Lowrance's product page for the Medium/High version: Medium and High CHIRP (83/200 kHz), DownScan 700/1200 kHz and SideScan 455/1075 kHz; the installation manual lists all four DownScan and SideScan frequencies as CHIRP. Lowrance publishes no beam angles. 2D is a forum estimate; the DownScan angles are estimates scaled by wavelength from a dealer's 45° at 800 kHz (a figure identical to Humminbird's published Down Imaging one); SideScan 1075 kHz is 455 kHz scaled the same way.2D sonar, full cone widthMedium CHIRP, 83 kHz?°One user on The Hull Truth forum, calculated from the 200 kHz figure; for the non-HD Active Imaging · confidence 2/5High CHIRP, 200 kHz?°Same forum user: \"around 20 degrees\"; no Lowrance source · confidence 2/5Cone angles must be between 0° and 120°.DownScan700 kHz CHIRP, fan side to side?°Estimate: dealer figure of 45° at 800 kHz × 800/700 · confidence 2/51200 kHz CHIRP, fan side to side?°Estimate: dealer figure of 45° at 800 kHz × 800/1200 · confidence 2/5Fan thickness, front to back?°Not published; an example · confidence 1/5Fan angles must be between 0° and 150°, the thickness between 0° and 30°.SideScan, each side455 kHz CHIRP, fan width?°Chosen so the fan reaches straight down (boulder test). A forum user quotes Lowrance support as 58° per side, without saying how it is aimed. · confidence 1/51075 kHz CHIRP, fan width?°Estimate: 455 kHz × 455/1075 · confidence 1/5Upper edge of the widest fan, below horizontal?°An example · confidence 1/5Thickness of the widest fan, front to back?°Not published; an example · confidence 1/5Narrower fans are aimed?Down to the same inner edge as the widest (no extra gap)Around the same center line (opens a gap under the boat)Not published. Objects straight under the boat showing on both sides at every frequency means the inner-edge choice matches your unit. Thickness scales with width either way.","html":"<p class=\"hint\" style=\"color:var(--fg)\">Frequencies from Lowrance's product page for the Medium/High version: Medium and High CHIRP (83/200 kHz), DownScan 700/1200 kHz and SideScan 455/1075 kHz; the installation manual lists all four DownScan and SideScan frequencies as CHIRP. Lowrance publishes no beam angles. 2D is a forum estimate; the DownScan angles are estimates scaled by wavelength from a dealer's 45° at 800 kHz (a figure identical to Humminbird's published Down Imaging one); SideScan 1075 kHz is 455 kHz scaled the same way.</p><div class=\"agrp\" data-eq=\"2d\"><h3>2D sonar, full cone width</h3><div class=\"arow\"><label for=\"cone0\">Medium CHIRP, 83 kHz<button type=\"button\" class=\"qm\" data-help=\"cone0\" aria-label=\"Show what this setting means\">?</button></label><div class=\"ain\"><input id=\"cone0\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"50\" data-save=\"\" data-def=\"50\"><span>°</span></div><p class=\"src mod\" data-src=\"cone0\">One user on The Hull Truth forum, calculated from the 200 kHz figure; for the non-HD Active Imaging · confidence 2/5</p></div><div class=\"arow\"><label for=\"cone1\">High CHIRP, 200 kHz<button type=\"button\" class=\"qm\" data-help=\"cone1\" aria-label=\"Show what this setting means\">?</button></label><div class=\"ain\"><input id=\"cone1\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"20\" data-save=\"\" data-def=\"20\"><span>°</span></div><p class=\"src\" data-src=\"cone1\">Same forum user: \"around 20 degrees\"; no Lowrance source · confidence 2/5</p></div><p class=\"err\" id=\"a2d-err\">Cone angles must be between 0° and 120°.</p></div><div class=\"agrp\" data-eq=\"ds\"><h3>DownScan</h3><div class=\"arow\"><label for=\"down0\">700 kHz CHIRP, fan side to side<button type=\"button\" class=\"qm\" data-help=\"down0\" aria-label=\"Show what this setting means\">?</button></label><div class=\"ain\"><input id=\"down0\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"51\" data-save=\"\" data-def=\"51\"><span>°</span></div><p class=\"src mod\" data-src=\"down0\">Estimate: dealer figure of 45° at 800 kHz × 800/700 · confidence 2/5</p></div><div class=\"arow\"><label for=\"down1\">1200 kHz CHIRP, fan side to side<button type=\"button\" class=\"qm\" data-help=\"down1\" aria-label=\"Show what this setting means\">?</button></label><div class=\"ain\"><input id=\"down1\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"30\" data-save=\"\" data-def=\"30\"><span>°</span></div><p class=\"src\" data-src=\"down1\">Estimate: dealer figure of 45° at 800 kHz × 800/1200 · confidence 2/5</p></div><div class=\"arow\"><label for=\"dst\">Fan thickness, front to back<button type=\"button\" class=\"qm\" data-help=\"dst\" aria-label=\"Show what this setting means\">?</button></label><div class=\"ain\"><input id=\"dst\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"3\" data-save=\"\" data-def=\"3\"><span>°</span></div><p class=\"src\" data-src=\"dst\">Not published; an example · confidence 1/5</p></div><p class=\"err\" id=\"ads-err\">Fan angles must be between 0° and 150°, the thickness between 0° and 30°.</p></div><div class=\"agrp\" data-eq=\"ss\"><h3>SideScan, each side</h3><div class=\"arow\"><label for=\"side0\">455 kHz CHIRP, fan width<button type=\"button\" class=\"qm\" data-help=\"side0\" aria-label=\"Show what this setting means\">?</button></label><div class=\"ain\"><input id=\"side0\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"85\" data-save=\"\" data-def=\"85\"><span>°</span></div><p class=\"src\" data-src=\"side0\">Chosen so the fan reaches straight down (boulder test). A forum user quotes Lowrance support as 58° per side, without saying how it is aimed. · confidence 1/5</p></div><div class=\"arow\"><label for=\"side1\">1075 kHz CHIRP, fan width<button type=\"button\" class=\"qm\" data-help=\"side1\" aria-label=\"Show what this setting means\">?</button></label><div class=\"ain\"><input id=\"side1\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"36\" data-save=\"\" data-def=\"36\"><span>°</span></div><p class=\"src\" data-src=\"side1\">Estimate: 455 kHz × 455/1075 · confidence 1/5</p></div><div class=\"arow\"><label for=\"sso\">Upper edge of the widest fan, below horizontal<button type=\"button\" class=\"qm\" data-help=\"sso\" aria-label=\"Show what this setting means\">?</button></label><div class=\"ain\"><input id=\"sso\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"5\" data-save=\"\" data-def=\"5\"><span>°</span></div><p class=\"src\" data-src=\"sso\">An example · confidence 1/5</p></div><div class=\"arow\"><label for=\"sst\">Thickness of the widest fan, front to back<button type=\"button\" class=\"qm\" data-help=\"sst\" aria-label=\"Show what this setting means\">?</button></label><div class=\"ain\"><input id=\"sst\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"2\" data-save=\"\" data-def=\"2\"><span>°</span></div><p class=\"src\" data-src=\"sst\">Not published; an example · confidence 1/5</p></div><div class=\"field\" style=\"padding-top:0.4rem\"><label for=\"ssalign\">Narrower fans are aimed<button type=\"button\" class=\"qm\" data-help=\"ssalign\" aria-label=\"Show what this setting means\">?</button></label><select id=\"ssalign\" class=\"sel\" data-save=\"\"><option value=\"inner\" selected=\"\">Down to the same inner edge as the widest (no extra gap)</option><option value=\"center\">Around the same center line (opens a gap under the boat)</option></select><p class=\"hint\">Not published. Objects straight under the boat showing on both sides at every frequency means the inner-edge choice matches your unit. Thickness scales with width either way.</p></div><p class=\"err\" id=\"ass-err\" hidden=\"\"></p></div>"},
